<speak>So your objective is to reduce your equity exposure and free up liquidity for the upcoming business expenses. I'll keep that in mind for this review. The market price of Summit Global Equity <sub alias="ee tee eff">ETF</sub> can fall when the underlying global equity markets decline. Also, if the market doesn't reach your minimum sale price, your sale may remain unfilled and delay access to the proceeds. Do you understand that the holding's price can fall with global equity markets, and that setting a minimum sale price could leave the sale unfilled?</speak>